## Deviation 1: the fold test is converted to PDF/X-1a

A plain `pdfunite` file fails `PRINT_GATE` on three checks: PDF version 1.4, no PDF/X marker, and
no output intent. The v18 fold test of `r6-v2` fails the same three checks (measured). Task line
1426 asks for a `PRINT_GATE` exit 0 on the fold-test file, so the maker converts it with
`make-pdfx.ts --k-only`, the same K-only conversion as the books. The text of pages 3 to 86 stays
equal to the v18 fold test (0 different pages), and the page count stays 86.

## Deviation 2: the drafts need --book-pages

As in `r6-v2`: the plan command of line 688 has no `--book-pages`, and without it the text gate
gives many differences. The build used the flag, and the gate gives 0 differences for each week.

